  "title": "Spellings",
  "emoji": "✏️",
  "parentNote": "Spellings need regular practice! Try the \"Look-Cover-Write-Check\" method: Look at the word, cover it, write it from memory, then check. Make spelling practice fun with word games and flashcards!",
  "learnBullets": [
    "Spelling common **everyday words** correctly",
    "Words related to **animals**, **body parts**, **clothes**, **food**, **emotions**",
    "Spotting the **correct spelling** among wrong options",
    "Finding the **wrongly spelled word** in a group"
  ],
  "learnItFirst": "**Why Spellings Matter:**\nIn the IEO exam, you might be asked to:\n1. Choose the correctly spelled word\n2. Find the wrongly spelled word\n3. Fill in the missing letters\n\n**Common Spelling Rules:**\n\n| Rule | Example |\n|------|---------|\n| \"i\" before \"e\" except after \"c\" | bel**ie**ve, rec**ei**ve |\n| Silent letters | **k**now, **w**rite, lis**t**en |\n| Double letters | happ**y** → happ**i**ness, runn**ing** |\n\n**Words You Must Know (Class 2 Level):**\n\n**Animals:** elephant, giraffe, monkey, rabbit, butterfly, parrot, tortoise\n\n**Body Parts:** shoulder, stomach, finger, tongue, knee, elbow, ankle\n\n**Clothes:** shirt, trousers, sweater, jacket, socks, shoes, dress\n\n**Food:** breakfast, biscuit, chocolate, vegetables, sandwich, juice\n\n**Emotions:** happy, angry, scared, excited, surprised, worried\n\n**School:** pencil, eraser, scissors, teacher, library, school\n\n---",
